{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>There they will offer sacrifices of righteousness.</b> That is, all will come to Mount Moriah because of their wealth, to offer sacrifices and to worship HaShem." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah, 'there they will offer sacrifices of righteousness' — he attributed the sacrifices to צדק, for צדק is the first recipient, and it is alluded to in the appended ה of המזבחה, and I have already mentioned this in the verse (Leviticus 1:9): והקטיר הכהן את הכל המזבחה." "<b>And the hidden treasures of sand.</b> He blessed them with wealth, with great abundance, that they should have vast riches and much wealth, until they would bury it in the sand. And the word ושפוני is as if it said וצפוני with a צ. And what it says, ושפוני טמוני, is a duplication of expression, like (Daniel 12:2) אדמת עפר. And Onkelos translated: וסימן דמטמרן בחלא מתגליין להון."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:54:13.792671007Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}